INT. VICTORIAN CONSERVATORY - NIGHT

A glass hothouse thick with tropical ferns, weeping under a gaslit chandelier. In its center, a round table draped in black velvet and ringed with four chairs. The air tastes of orchids and old rain.

MRS. CRABTREE (60s, widow's weeds, a face like a locked door) presides at the head of the table. THADDEUS (30s, frock coat, spectacles, a pamphlet on spiritualism rolled in his fist) sits at her right. PHOEBE (20s, white lace, pale as milk, hands folded) sits at her left. CAPTAIN LOWRY (50s, red-faced, medals on his tunic, arms folded in contempt) sits opposite.

MRS. CRABTREE
Join hands. And do try to behave, Captain.

CAPTAIN LOWRY
I am the soul of decorum, madam.

PHOEBE
Is it true they come when called?

THADDEUS
Only if they have unfinished business.

CAPTAIN LOWRY
Then they'll be here by the dozen. The dead always have unfinished business.

MRS. CRABTREE
Silence.

They clasp hands. The chandelier dims. The ferns sway though no wind moves. Somewhere in the glass, a pane creaks.

MRS. CRABTREE (CONT'D)
Spirits of this house, we call upon you. If you are present, give us a sign.

A silence. A drip. Another.

THADDEUS
(whispering)
Nothing.

CAPTAIN LOWRY
Of course nothing.

PHOEBE
Hush. Listen.

MRS. CRABTREE
We call upon Edmund Crabtree, my beloved husband.

CAPTAIN LOWRY
Your late husband was a bore, madam, and I say that as one who attended his funeral.

MRS. CRABTREE
Captain, I will have you removed.

CAPTAIN LOWRY
By whom?

A tap on the table. A second. A third. The four of them freeze. The candle flames bend flat. The temperature drops; their breath fogs.

PHOEBE
(barely audible)
Who is it?

The table lifts an inch. Settles. Lifts again. Thaddeus lets go of the hands to steady it, and Mrs. Crabtree slaps him across the knuckles.

MRS. CRABTREE
Do not break the circle!

THADDEUS
It's moving!

CAPTAIN LOWRY
It's a trick, madam. It's always a trick.

A voice, wheezing, not any of theirs, slithers from beneath the velvet.

CAPTAIN LOWRY (O.S.)
Hortensia...

MRS. CRABTREE
Edmund?

Phoebe screams. Thaddeus leaps back. Mrs. Crabtree sits perfectly rigid, her face as pale as the lace on Phoebe's collar. Then the velvet lifts, and the Captain, still seated, lets the cloth fall from his lap. His boot withdraws from the table's leg. He coughs into his fist, and the wheeze is plainly his own.

PHOEBE
That was you!

CAPTAIN LOWRY
A bit of fun, miss.

Mrs. Crabtree rises to her full height.

MRS. CRABTREE
Captain Lowry. You are no longer welcome in my home.

CAPTAIN LOWRY
It was only a joke.

MRS. CRABTREE
So was Edmund.
